> the square of x plus y
  note: what does "the square of" apply to: read as (x)^2 + ..., not (x + ...)^2 (say "the square of the quantity ..." for the second)
  ucas: it(x, y) = x^2 + y
  ucas: show it
it(x: real, y: real) = x^2 + y
  -> real
> the square root of x plus 1
  note: what does "the square root of" apply to: read as sqrt(x) + ..., not sqrt(x + ...) (say "the square root of the quantity ..." for the second)
  ucas: it(x) = sqrt(x) + 1
  ucas: show it
it(x: real) = sqrt(x) + 1
  -> real
> the sum of x and y squared
  note: what does "squared/power" apply to: read as ... + y^2, not (... + y)^2 (say "the square of the sum of ..." for the second)
  ucas: it(x, y) = x + y^2
  ucas: show it
it(x: real, y: real) = x + y^2
  -> real
> 7/8 of 64
  ucas: 7/8*64
56
> wrap of x+1
  ucas: it(x) = x + 1
  ucas: wrap it
wrap analysis of it:
  no wrapping or rounding operations
  end to end vs the real-number result: max abs error 0, max rel error 0
  over all 101 points of the domain
